00:29:41.390 --> 00:29:42.110
You know what was that fast?

00:29:42.410 --> 00:29:42.890
Not really.

00:29:42.970 --> 00:29:43.370
I'll tell you what.

00:29:43.430 --> 00:29:45.250
The old car really run good, but it worked good.

00:29:45.290 --> 00:29:46.450
That's what really surprised me.

00:29:46.570 --> 00:29:48.910
It looked like Darrell and Ed was running up the racetrack behind me.

00:29:49.230 --> 00:29:50.870
They could run up to me down the straightaway.

00:29:50.950 --> 00:29:53.850
When I get to the corner, they'd slide up, and I could stay on the bottom real good.

00:29:53.930 --> 00:29:56.050
I saw you coming down low on the backstretch a lot.

00:29:56.170 --> 00:29:58.310
Was that a little maneuver you were doing there?

00:29:58.430 --> 00:29:59.510
I was trying to keep them racing.

00:29:59.510 --> 00:29:59.910
and father.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:03.480
by side. That's what I was trying to do, and I did a good job on that. Tell us about that

00:30:03.840 --> 00:30:07.900
first lap episode. Were you close to that? Did you see what happened? No, not really. I looked up

00:30:07.900 --> 00:30:12.560
in the mirror, and I saw Labonte sideways, and I just got out of the alley because I thought

00:30:12.560 --> 00:30:16.340
they'd just totally restart the race, and then all them other cars went by me, and I called in

00:30:16.340 --> 00:30:20.940
and asked Ernie. He said, well, he said, you're where you at. I said, oh, okay, so we'll go from

00:30:20.940 --> 00:30:24.700
there. Everybody's got to be someplace. What does this mean for next Sunday, Bill? Well, it means a

00:30:24.700 --> 00:30:28.220
lot. You know, come in here and do this. You know, it looked like a lot of people had a lot of trouble

00:30:28.220 --> 00:30:29.980
coming into the race because I don't

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:33.580
I think the lack of practice and all that stuff seemed to have hindered a lot of teams.

00:30:33.800 --> 00:30:36.500
You know, I felt like I was pretty much ready, because when I came down here and tested,

00:30:36.620 --> 00:30:39.600
I tried to run several laps, and the car really worked good.

00:30:40.700 --> 00:30:43.540
Philly, you know, you've never run as fast as this before in your life,

00:30:43.540 --> 00:30:45.080
and you've never talked this fast before.

00:30:45.700 --> 00:30:47.960
Congratulations, and good luck on the 500 next Sunday.

00:30:48.160 --> 00:30:50.140
And now, let's go upstairs to Ken Spryer.

00:30:51.180 --> 00:30:54.140
Fifteen minutes, ten seconds was the time to run this one off,

00:30:54.180 --> 00:30:58.540
standing alongside a two-time winner of the class, who hopes so much to be out here today.

00:30:58.760 --> 00:30:59.980
He'll be carrying one of our seats.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:02.060
CBS in-car cameras next week

00:31:02.060 --> 00:31:04.020
in the Daytona 500. What about next

00:31:04.020 --> 00:31:06.140
week, Neil Bonnet? Ken, well, the handwriting's on the

00:31:06.140 --> 00:31:08.180
wall. We've got our work to do this week to get prepared

00:31:08.180 --> 00:31:10.120
for the 500. Bill's shown us the Ford

00:31:10.120 --> 00:31:12.060
superiority in the corner, and we've got some

00:31:12.060 --> 00:31:14.100
Chevrolets and Pontiacs, I think, can get after them, so we've

00:31:14.100 --> 00:31:16.590
got to go to work. Any surprises here today

00:31:16.590 --> 00:31:18.590
in this race for you, Neil? Well, I was, uh,

00:31:18.670 --> 00:31:20.610
I wanted to see the strength of Bill Elliott. I think that

00:31:20.610 --> 00:31:22.810
everybody in this garage has wondered how strong he was,

00:31:22.910 --> 00:31:24.890
and after that kind of a fluke start

00:31:24.890 --> 00:31:26.650
of the race, and he made him go back in the rear

00:31:26.650 --> 00:31:28.770
and come up there, he had to show his hand, and it's

00:31:28.770 --> 00:31:29.850
as strong as everybody thought.

00:31:30.440 --> 00:31:31.820
Thank you very much, Neil Bonnet.

00:31:31.920 --> 00:31:35.520
You'll see him in the Raymott car next week here in the Daytona 500.

00:31:35.910 --> 00:31:39.330
We'll be back with more from the World Center of Speed right after the...

00:31:39.670 --> 00:31:40.990
Right to Chris Econimacki.

00:31:41.730 --> 00:31:44.090
This race is a big head start on the Daytona 500.

00:31:44.290 --> 00:31:46.510
Those who didn't win, no, they have a lot of work to do.

00:31:46.630 --> 00:31:50.270
But let's not lose sight of what happened on the track here today.

00:31:50.430 --> 00:31:53.770
In an age where drivers have to be corporate spokespeople,

00:31:54.750 --> 00:31:56.830
financiers, and public relations practitioners,

00:31:57.070 --> 00:31:59.970
it's nice to know that and refreshing to watch...

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:08.740
with old boyhood boats my car is faster than your car was run so it's out of the 500 next Sunday

00:32:08.740 --> 00:32:13.890
no other sport has its most important race at the very beginning of the season and what we saw

00:32:13.890 --> 00:32:23.050
today was a clash and what we're going to see next Sunday is a war a harbinger of things to

00:32:23.050 --> 00:32:27.650
come for sure Ford is the car to watch for in the 500 next week Bill Elliott has proven that

00:32:27.650 --> 00:32:29.410
as we take a look at the final standings

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:31.940
coming in second, Waltrip in third.

00:32:32.180 --> 00:32:36.420
Ricky Rudd finishing in 10th after his car went out early from the event.

00:32:36.560 --> 00:32:40.440
Terry Labonte also having problems in that very first lap skirmish.

00:32:41.040 --> 00:32:44.380
For Chris Iconimaki, Ned Jarrett, and Mike Joy.
